You have two choices, depending on what you mean by “I don't want Business Consultant AI anymore.”

Option 1: Delete only the Business Consultant AI Agent

If you want to keep your Google Cloud project for other work, such as your other AI projects, delete only the deployed Vertex AI Agent Engine resource.

Google officially supports deleting the Agent Engine instance, including child resources when force=True.

In Google Cloud Console, go to Vertex AI → Agent Engine / deployed agents, find your Business Consultant AI, and choose Delete. Google also documents deletion of deployed agents from the console.

This is probably the best option for you if the same Google Cloud project contains other projects or resources you still need.

Option 2: Delete the entire Google Cloud project

If you created a separate project only for:

Business Consultant AI

then you can shut down/delete the entire project.

Google states that deleting the project removes the resources associated with that project. A shut-down project can generally be restored during a waiting period before permanent deletion.

Important ⚠️

Before deleting the whole project, check whether you also have:

Vertex AI agents
Cloud Storage buckets
deployed website/backend
APIs
databases
other projects or experiments

inside that same Google Cloud Project.

My recommendation

Since you have been using Google Cloud for multiple AI learning projects, do not immediately delete the entire Google Cloud project. First check the project resources, then delete only Business Consultant AI / its Agent Engine deployment if that is the only thing you no longer want.

